    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d526">

                <pb facs="0511" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/5269: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-26T16:00:00+02:00">August 26, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>474. My 464, August 21, 8 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d526-f1"/> There have been
                    no further flights of Russian planes over Moldavia. Discussing this matter with
                    the Prime Minister yesterday he seemed to feel that relations with Russia might
                    be quiescent for the present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
